,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear","html_url":"https://github.com/linear","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/linear/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Linear","description":"","external_url":"https://linear.app","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/linear","created_at":"2018-11-02T18:07:23Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T00:40:30Z","permissions":{"checks":"read","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_suite","issues","issue_comment","label","pull_request","pull_request_review","repository","sub_issues"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3938258016","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3938258016","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3938258016,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7qvQxg","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T06:12:32Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T06:12:32Z","body":"This is something we were going to look into, but haven't yet\n\nAutocomplete can be used as a [filterable menu](https://base-ui.com/react/components/autocomplete#command-palette), but it has no support for nested submenus. It's undecided how the API for submenus will look right now.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3938258016/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3939205014","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3939205014","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3939205014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7qy3-W","user":{"login":"brunobely","id":4048689,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNDg2ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4048689?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely","html_url":"https://github.com/brunobely","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/brunobely/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-21T18:23:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-21T18:23:00Z","body":"Hm, I wonder if I can Frankenstein Autocomplete and Menu together for now as a workaround","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3939205014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940009326","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3940009326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3940009326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7q18Vu","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T03:05:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T03:05:09Z","body":"It can work provided the menu with a search filter has no submenu triggers as items, otherwise it won't by default. You'd need to fire keyboard events on the virtually-focused item (that has `data-highlighted` while the input has DOM focus) to trigger a click on the submenu trigger to open its submenu","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940009326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940071457","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3940071457","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3940071457,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7q2Lgh","user":{"login":"CiscoFran10","id":85837405,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODM3NDA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85837405?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10","html_url":"https://github.com/CiscoFran10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T03:40:08Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T03:49:33Z","body":"@brunobely\n\nThis is as far as I was able to get in terms of matching Linear’s behavior. It’s close, but still not fully correct.\n\nThe main issue I haven’t been able to resolve cleanly is making the search input autofocus when hovering menus/submenus without breaking keyboard navigation. I tried composing Menu with Autocomplete and Combobox, but I couldn’t get the keyboard interactions to remain consistent with Linear’s especially for nested submenus.\n\nAlso, I believe the ARIA for this could be wrong too, since Linear’s filter component uses the listbox/option roles for the menu and items, and the Menu component renders menu/menuitem as roles. So I think Combobox or Autocomplete might be more correct for this case.\n\nHere’s a reproduction:\n\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/tnzbz8eh-ey1njnfn?file=src%2FApp.tsx\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940071457/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940086123","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3940086123","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3940086123,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7q2PFr","user":{"login":"CiscoFran10","id":85837405,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg1ODM3NDA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/85837405?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10","html_url":"https://github.com/CiscoFran10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/CiscoFran10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T03:54:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T03:54:45Z","body":"@atomiks Ariakit has a good example on what I believe @brunobely wants. https://ariakit.org/examples/menu-nested-combobox\n\nIt composes their Menu component with a Combobox component. \n\n<img width=\"627\" height=\"532\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/253d62de-b0a8-44e7-9fba-9850c71bcd5a\" />","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940086123/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940091758","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3940091758","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3940091758,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7q2Qdu","user":{"login":"atomiks","id":22450188,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNDUwMTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22450188?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks","html_url":"https://github.com/atomiks","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/atomiks/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-22T04:00:37Z","updated_at":"2026-02-22T04:09:25Z","body":"Yep, I know of that one, but the API to compose them gets really complex.\n\nAs you mentioned, the `combobox` + `option` role is [more compatible across screen readers](https://x.com/diegohaz/status/1947336727158227056) (what Linear uses), so it's more like Autocomplete needs `SubmenuRoot` parts, rather than Menu needing an `Input` part. DX wise (what a user might expect from the component) this is kind of inverted though — it makes more intuitive sense to stick an input in a Menu and it just works. This is why we had a separate (unshipped) `FilterableMenu` component  in the original Combobox/Autocomplete PR. A separate component with different roles and behavior is probably \"cleanest\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3940091758/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3950038099","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-3950038099","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":3950038099,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7rcMxT","user":{"login":"rohanchkrabrty","id":29628929,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5NjI4OTI5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29628929?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty","html_url":"https://github.com/rohanchkrabrty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rohanchkrabrty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T08:32:34Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T21:18:29Z","body":"I built something similar using `Menu` + `Autocomplete` [Preview here](https://apsara-ikqpeob98-raystack.vercel.app/docs/components/menu#autocomplete)\n\nI had to manually trigger focus events to make it work. There are still a few rough edges, but overall it works well.\n\n@atomiks From a DX point of view, it might be worth adding built-in support for this in Menu, even tho it might not be the cleanest. It would be very helpful if this feature was supported natively.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3950038099/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/4222864774","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-4222864774","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":4222864774,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs77s82G","user":{"login":"oleksandrkovaliuk","id":133936726,"node_id":"U_kgDOB_u2Vg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/133936726?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk","html_url":"https://github.com/oleksandrkovaliuk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oleksandrkovaliuk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-10T10:29:48Z","updated_at":"2026-04-10T10:29:48Z","body":"Jumping in with an example that uses a Combobox within DropdownContent (SubContent) - for cases where you need memorable selections and other Combobox goodies and therefore can't use Autocomplete.\n\nCheck out a quick [Preview](https://stackblitz.com/edit/vitejs-vite-ppbxpzec?file=src%2FApp.tsx)\n\n```tsx\n            <DropdownMenuSub loopFocus>\n              <DropdownMenuSubTrigger delay={0}>\n                {selectedState?.label || \"Select State\"}\n              </DropdownMenuSubTrigger>\n\n              <DropdownMenuSubContent\n                //  role=\"dialog\" overrides the default role=\"menu\" to allow non-menu-item children (combobox) without violating ARIA content model\n                role=\"dialog\"\n                className=\"w-52\"\n                // Focus the input on hover so combobox keyboard bindings stay responsive\n                onPointerEnter={focusComboboxInput}\n              >\n                <StateCombobox\n                  // needed to allow correct keyboard navigation and enter key selection\n                  open\n                  inline\n                  value={selectedState?.value || \"\"}\n                  onValueChange={(currentValue, eventDetails) => {\n                    onStateChange(currentValue?.value);\n                    // Prevents popup-like close behavior so filtering stays responsive\n                    // during inline combobox rendering\n                    eventDetails.cancel();\n                  }}\n                  countryCode={selectedCountry?.value as CountryCode}\n                >\n                  <ComboboxInput\n                    autoFocus\n                    onKeyDown={(e) => {\n                      // Allow Escape, ArrowLeft (at pos 0), and Tab to bubble up to\n                      // the menu for submenu close / back-navigation / focus management.\n                      // Block everything else so menu's typeahead and list navigation\n                      // don't intercept combobox keystrokes.\n                      if (e.key === \"Escape\") return;\n                      if (\n                        e.key === \"ArrowLeft\" &&\n                        e.currentTarget.selectionStart === 0\n                      )\n                        return;\n                      if (e.key === \"Tab\") return;\n                      e.stopPropagation();\n                    }}\n                    placeholder=\"Search State\"\n                  />\n\n                  <ComboboxEmpty>No options available.</ComboboxEmpty>\n\n                  <StateComboboxList />\n                </StateCombobox>\n              </DropdownMenuSubContent>\n            </DropdownMenuSub>\n```\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/4222864774/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/4910006160","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-4910006160","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":4910006160,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABJKi_kA","user":{"login":"twillhorn","id":8485001,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg0ODUwMDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8485001?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn","html_url":"https://github.com/twillhorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/twillhorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-07T23:41:05Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T23:41:05Z","body":"I have such a use case. Embedding the input in a Menu.Item (render) works, but we needed a stack of workarounds to keep it usable:\n\n1. **Typeahead capture** — useTypeahead's onKeyDown consumes any printable key reaching the popup, with no editable-target guard, so typing in the input jump-highlights items and swallows characters. We stopPropagation on keydown from the input's item to keep keys out of typeahead.\n2. **IME composition** — with focus-follows-hover active, pointer movement during composition refocuses the popup and drops the composition session. We set highlightItemOnHover={false} on that submenu (the paths in useListNavigation are gated on focusItemOnHover, so this works).\n3. **Lost hover affordance** — as a consequence of (2), no row in that submenu gets a pointer-driven [data-highlighted], so plain items and submenu triggers show no hover feedback. We stamp rows of such submenus with a data attribute and recreate the hover styling in CSS, including a [data-popup-open] variant for submenu triggers because they lose :hover to the pointer-capture backdrop once their flyout opens.\n4. (Now fixed — thanks!) On ≤1.5.0 the submenu trigger's onMouseEnter ignored highlightItemOnHover={false}, which left a stale data-highlighted on the trigger after its flyout closed since nothing could move the highlight off it. #4892 in 1.6.0 resolved this.\n\nAll symptoms of the same gap: there's no supported way to tell Menu \"this popup contains an editable element; suspend typeahead and focus-follows-hover around it, but keep highlight behavior for the other rows.\" A Menu.Input (or an official Combobox-inside-Menu composition) that handles typeahead suspension, focus/IME safety, and preserves per-item highlight for siblings would let us delete all of it.\n\nHappy to provide more detail or test a canary if it helps.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/4910006160/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/5928693586","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/4157#issuecomment-5928693586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/4157","id":5928693586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs8AAAABYWCvUg","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%